## 4. Leaky-ReLU plateau = weight explosion

### Section 4.3, line 161 (first two sentences), and Section 6, line 297

**Current (161):**
> "Leaky-ReLU shows a different pattern. All 30 runs have their largest one-epoch loss increase
> at epochs 13--15."

**Problem.** The mechanism is now measured:
- the output weight norm grows by orders of magnitude in one epoch;
- the softmax saturates;
- units do not die;
- the run then sits at a plateau whose loss is the clamp value (item 1);
- the spike epoch is nearly fixed by (H, LR), but no single pre-spike quantity predicts it.

**Evidence.** [E-S0] `mechanism_tables/q4_leaky_spikes.csv`, `q4_spike_epoch_spread.csv`,
`q4_spike_predictors.csv`, `q4_spike_recovery.csv`; figure `mech_q4_leaky_spike`.

