## Outline: new section "What happens inside a collapsing network" (\label{sec:mechanism})

Replaces most of Section 6 (lines 290-301); keep line 291 (bounded vs linear path), line 299
(tanh caveat) and line 301 (width and update size).

1. **Probes.** What is recorded per epoch:
   - activation statistics on 1,000 fixed validation inputs (dead = z ≤ 0 on all of them;
     tanh saturation |z| > 3);
   - weight norms and relative updates per layer;
   - logit spread across inputs.

   Dead on the probe set is not dead on the training set (revival, paragraph 3).
   *Cites:* none (methods).
2. **ReLU collapse = last hidden layer dies; fast.**
   - Stage 0: hidden2 dead {{mechanism.q1.s0_h128_lr0.03.dead_last_final_med:.2f}}, hidden1 {{mechanism.q1.s0_h128_lr0.03.dead_first_final_med:.3f}}.
   - 10 % to 90 % dead within ≤ 1 epoch in {{mechanism.q1.speed.all.share_le1:pct0}} % of collapses.
   - Slower at H256 ({{report.speed.s2_h256.share_le1:pct0}} % ≤ 1 epoch).
   - 90 % dead reached in the epoch of e* in {{report.speed.e90_at_estar}}.

   *Cites:* figure `mech_q1_event_study`, `q1_relu_collapse.csv`, `q1_collapse_speed.csv`.
3. **Revival.**
   - {{mechanism.q1.revival.n_revived}} of {{mechanism.q1.revival.n_revived:n}} CIFAR-10/MNIST runs with a ≥ 99 % dead layer revive, all on CIFAR-10.
   - Revival goes with conv-weight updates (median {{mechanism.q1.revival.dw_conv_median_revived:.3f}} vs
     {{mechanism.q1.revival.dw_conv_median_not_revived:.4f}}).

   *Cites:* `q1_revival_summary.csv`, `q1_revival_runs.csv`.
4. **Hybrid: two regimes.**
   - Protected: ReLU half alive, at LR 0.03 ({{mechanism.q2.s0_h128_lr0.03.hybrid_relu_dead_hidden2:.3f}} dead).
   - Carried: ReLU half dead and the tanh half working, at LR 0.05 ({{mechanism.q2.s0_h128_lr0.05.hybrid_relu_dead_hidden2:.2f}}).
   - The CIFAR-10 CNN at LR 0.02 is mostly carried ({{report.q2.cifar10_cnn_lr0.02.carried}}).

   *Cites:* figure `mech_q2_hybrid_dead`, `q2_hybrid_regimes.csv`, `q2_regime_switch.csv`.
5. **Leaky ReLU: weight explosion, not dead units.**
   - Output weight norm ×{{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.03.jump_output_med:.2g}}.
   - Saturated softmax; loss = clamp × error.
   - Spike timing fixed by (H, LR), ICC {{mechanism.q4.spread.s0_mnist_mlp2.icc:.3f}}.
   - No single predictor.
   - Plateau mlp2-specific.

   *Cites:* figure `mech_q4_leaky_spike`, `q4_leaky_spikes.csv`, `q4_spike_epoch_spread.csv`,
   `q4_spike_predictors.csv`, `q4_clamp_check.csv`, `q4_spike_recovery.csv`.
6. **No reliable early warning.**
   - The loss rise precedes failure in {{mechanism.q6.lossrise.all.share_fires_before_failure:pct0}} % of failing runs.
   - It is a false positive in {{mechanism.q6.lossrise.all.fpr_same_cells:pct0}} % of stable runs of the same cells.
   - AUCs {{mechanism.q6.s2.loss_rise.auc:.2f}}-{{mechanism.q6.s0.dw_spike.auc:.2f}}.
   - Use the paper sentence in `FINDINGS_partA.md` §3.

   *Cites:* figure `mech_q6_lead_times`, `q6_auc.csv`, `q6_loss_rise_reconcile.csv`.
7. **Depth.**
   - Late collapse needs two rectified layers.
   - mlp1 ReLU: {{outcomes.depth.v6_stage2.mnist.mlp1.relu.n_late_collapse}} / {{outcomes.depth.v6_stage2.cifar10.mlp1.relu.n_late_collapse}} late collapses.

   *Cites:* `outcomes/depth_check.csv`, `outcomes/depth_matched_stage2.csv`.

